  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "English | [简体中文](./README.zh.md)"
    },
    {
      "section": "Cyrus Plugins · @cyrusdoyle/dsh-plugins",
      "text": "A plugin collection for DeepSeek Harness (DSH). Install this one bundle to get every plugin listed below; each plugin can also be installed on its own."
    },
    {
      "section": "Plugins",
      "text": "| Plugin                                                 | npm package                  | What it does                                                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------------------------------------------ | ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| [Sessions Insight](./plugins/sessions-insight/README.md) | `@cyrusdoyle/dsh-sessions-insight` | Opens up what each turn of a Claude Code, DSH or Codex session actually fed the model: composition, tool calls, compactions, cost. Includes confirmed session deletion. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Requires DSH 0.2.1-rc.5 or newer (see `docs/adr/0002-asar-021-is-the-contract.md`). First decide which profile to install into: the desktop app uses `desktop`, `dsh web` on the command line uses `web`. Installing into the wrong profile does not error; the plugin just never shows up.\n\n**Install the collection (recommended)** to get every plugin at once; when a plugin is added to the collection later, upgrading the collection brings it in."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin --profile desktop add @cyrusdoyle/dsh-plugins   # desktop app\ndsh plugin --profile web     add @cyrusdoyle/dsh-plugins   # dsh web\n```\n\n**Install a single plugin**:\n\n```bash\ndsh plugin --profile desktop add @cyrusdoyle/dsh-sessions-insight   # desktop app\ndsh plugin --profile web     add @cyrusdoyle/dsh-sessions-insight   # dsh web\n```\n\nThen **fully quit and reopen** DSH. \"Cyrus Plugins\" or \"Sessions Insight\" in the plugin manager means it worked."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "> **Pick one of the two.** The collection and the standalone plugin insert the same id into the loader tree; with both in `dsh.profile.bundles`, DSH fails at boot with `duplicate loader entry id`. Run `dsh plugin --profile <name> remove` on one before switching to the other.\n>\n> **Git installs work for the standalone plugin, not for the collection.** `plugins/sessions-insight/lib/` is committed, so the member can be installed straight from this repository without running build scripts — for example `dsh plugin --profile desktop add github:Mt-Youya/dsh-plugins#path:/plugins/sessions-insight`, or point the plugin manager at a local checkout of that directory. The collection cannot be installed from Git: its root `dependencies` use `workspace:^`, which is only rewritten to a version number by `pnpm pack` / publish. Install the collection from npm, or link this checkout as described below."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "**Installing from this working tree (developing the collection)**: the desktop plugin manager's \"Add plugin\" also accepts a local directory — point it at this checkout's absolute path. DSH records it as `\"@cyrusdoyle/dsh-plugins\": \"link:<that path>\"`: a symlink into your working tree, not a copy, and nothing is built for you. The host resolves `lib/index.js` through that link, and `lib/` is gitignored, so build it first (the collection embeds the compiled stylesheet, so the CSS step comes first):"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```bash\nnode scripts/build-css.mjs plugins/sessions-insight && npx tsdown --minify\n```\n\nThen fully quit and reopen DSH. Later edits only need a rebuild and a restart — there is no need to reinstall.\n\nEach plugin's usage, permission boundary and known limitations live in its own README."
    },
    {
      "section": "Settings, balance and update checks",
      "text": "The collection embeds the same plugin source as the standalone member (ADR 0009), so its runtime behaviour is the Sessions Insight behaviour: read-only insight, the handoff, confirmed session deletion, plus a settings page and two opt-in utilities."
    },
    {
      "section": "Settings, balance and update checks",
      "text": "- **Settings are saved by the Host.** `/api/dsh-sessions-insight/settings` is read-only; the six switches (session overview, Skills tab, cumulative level chart, expand tools by default, balance display, automatic version checks) are written through the Host's configuration form and stored by the Host. The plugin writes no config file.\n- **Balance and version checks are off by default.** Turning one on — or pressing its button — is the only thing that makes the plugin call out. Outbound traffic is limited to two fixed HTTPS endpoints, `https://api.deepseek.com/user/balance` and `https://registry.npmjs.org/@cyrusdoyle%2F.../latest`, with no redirects, no cookies and no caller-controlled URL.\n- **Credentials**: the balance check resolves the credential reference configured for the DeepSeek official adapter (`apiKeyEnv`, default `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`), then falls back to the signed-in DeepSeek account. Custom provider references are not followed; the plugin never stores or logs the key.\n- **The read surface never rewrites source logs.** The only writes are the handoff routes — `handoff/apply` delivers a brief through the official `session.create` + `session.prompt`, `handoff/reveal` creat"
    },
    {
      "section": "Settings, balance and update checks",
      "text": "The plugin README has the full route list, defaults and known limitations."
    },
    {
      "section": "Repository layout",
      "text": "This is a pnpm monorepo. Only the collection and `plugins/*` are published; the rest is inlined into the plugins at build time."
    },
    {
      "section": "Repository layout",
      "text": "| Path                         | Contents                                                                  | Published                             |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `/` (root)                   | The collection bundle: `cordis.patch.yml`, `locale/`, its own `lib/`      | **yes**, `@cyrusdoyle/dsh-plugins`         |\n| `plugins/sessions-insight`    | The Sessions Insight plugin: host half and browser half                       | **yes**, `@cyrusdoyle/dsh-sessions-insight` |\n| `packages/session-contract`  | The unified IR, wire types and their guards                               | no                                    |\n| `packages/session-readers`   | Claude Code / Codex / DSH readers                                         | no                                    |\n| `packages/plugin-kit`        | Plugin-agnostic JSON envelope and URL spelling                            | no                                    |\n| `packages/plugin-kit-host`   | Host-half plumbing: route table, same-origin gate, envelope, LRU          | no                              "
    },
    {
      "section": "Repository layout",
      "text": "Dependencies point one way only: `plugins/* → packages/*`. The package-name-to-source mapping lives in `tooling/aliases.ts`, and `tsconfig.json`'s `paths` mirrors it, so tests, the preview app and the build never need the internal packages built first."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```bash\npnpm install\n```\n\n```bash\npnpm dev\n```\n\nThe preview runs at <http://localhost:5178> and reads your real local sessions; add `?theme=light` or `?theme=dark` to switch themes.\n\nRun the gates before you commit:\n\n```bash\nnpx tsc --noEmit && npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.client.json && npx vitest run && node scripts/build-css.mjs plugins/sessions-insight && npx tsdown --minify && node scripts/check-bundle.mjs plugins/sessions-insight && node scripts/check-bundle.mjs .\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "CI runs the same gates and additionally fails when the committed `plugins/sessions-insight/lib/` differs from a rebuild — see [`.github/workflows/ci.yml`](./.github/workflows/ci.yml).\n\nRebuild the artifacts and check that the profile's link really points at your build (this does not install — installation happens in the DSH plugin manager):\n\n```bash\npnpm install:plugin\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "Regenerate the README screenshots from the preview (headless Chrome, 1440×900; add `-- --theme light` for the light theme). They show the sessions on your machine, so look at them before committing:\n\n```bash\npnpm screenshots\n```\n\nOptional browser checks (need a local Chrome; not part of CI):\n\n- `pnpm smoke:preview` measures the mounted panel in both themes under `?probe=1`.\n- `pnpm check:ui` drives the session-menu interactions against a fixture server."
    },
    {
      "section": "Publishing",
      "text": "Follow [`docs/RELEASE.md`](./docs/RELEASE.md): the member and the collection share one version number and are published together, member first (ADR 0010)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Documentation",
      "text": "- [`docs/RELEASE.md`](./docs/RELEASE.md) — publishing to npm\n- `docs/PLAN.md` — decisions and milestones (Chinese)\n- `docs/IR.md` — the unified turn IR, the adapter contract (Chinese)\n- `docs/API.md` — host route contract (Chinese)\n- `docs/HANDOFF.md` — handoff contract (Chinese)\n- `docs/adr/` — architecture decision records (Chinese)\n- `GLOSSARY.md` — vocabulary (Chinese)"
    },
